msgid "Camera Controls and Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:7
#: 910f1c06b4044e6ab1385de59c1be79a
msgid "This page provides an overview of general camera setup parameters and the three different ways that cameras can be controlled.  The related page detailing :ref:`gimbal controls can be found here <common-mount-targeting>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:10
#: 601a184338c94facbb60ab7d8d937923
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:12
#: f75990b3a8cf45f2b7e86218a8836a0d
msgid "ArduPilot supports up to two cameras. The following is for the first camera:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:14
#: 6ead670db63e44399837ba35e7a43c53
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_TYPE<CAM1_TYPE>`: Camera shutter (trigger) type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:15
#: 57eaaefd14984ce68b6b092d6de0adb4
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_DURATION<CAM1_DURATION>`: Camera open shutter duration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:16
#: f7748fd11fa041a6a9280ea26910644d
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_SERVO_ON<CAM1_SERVO_ON>`: Camera servo ON PWM value (Servo type shutter only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:17
#: 647903a4ba684a74abdef09c6ab600e8
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_SERVO_OFF<CAM1_SERVO_OFF>`: Camera servo OFF PWM value (Servo type shutter only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:18
#: eb554a6a13b3404f8daad604065bf4e3
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_TRIGG_DIST<CAM1_TRIGG_DIST>`: Camera trigger distance. If this value is non-zero then the camera will trigger whenever the position changes by this number of meters regardless of what mode the autopilot is in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:19
#: 5fd169092f2145e9b2eb04796bdd0870
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_RELAY_ON<CAM1_RELAY_ON>`: Camera relay ON value. This sets whether the relay goes high or low when it triggers. Note that you should also set RELAY_DEFAULT appropriately for your camera(Relay type shutter only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:20
#: 0debb9ad77284e0686bf45397a1506d3
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_INTRVAL_MIN<CAM1_INTRVAL_MIN>`: Camera minimum time interval between photos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:21
#: 79f684b0f63c4ba2aba56a00b886e593
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_MNT_INST<CAM1_MNT_INST>`: If the camera is associated with a MOUNTx instance, this indicates which MOUNTx instance. For example if CAM1 is associated with MOUNT2, then this value will be 2. The default value of 0 for this parameter means that the Mount instance is the same as the Camera instance, ie. CAM1 is in MOUNT1 and is the same as value \"1\" in this case. This allows Camera commands to be directed to the correct MOUNT instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:22
#: 7eb19a6942d54eb6ba96ecb6dc18bbe2
msgid ":ref:`CAM1_OPTIONS<CAM1_OPTIONS>`: if bit 0 set and camera/mount has the ability to start/stop video recording, then it will start on arm and stop on disarm events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:25
#: 0cde011e6b7f4eda9f834bd4a5dadfcc
msgid "be sure to set the ``CAMx_INTRVAL_MIN`` to be greater than the fastest the camera can take photos when using the camera trigger functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:27
#: 07f457c605de428daf2d764fbde8355d
msgid ":ref:`CAM_MAX_ROLL<CAM_MAX_ROLL>`: Maximum photo roll angle. Postpone shooting if roll is greater than limit. (0=Disable, will shoot regardless of roll)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:28
#: 2c121c5d124844a284c7fb3d3317d5de
msgid ":ref:`CAM_AUTO_ONLY<CAM_AUTO_ONLY>`: Distance-triggering in AUTO mode only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:31
#: 699079bbff934c34a06e078e77587a03
msgid "Control with an RC transmitter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-camera-controls.rst:33
#: 2db3fc5bf8f94405814c2ef637a689b8
